# Observatory adoption

This repository records one explicit command through the pinned
[Observatory instrumentation action](https://github.com/emmett08/observatory-instrumentation/tree/[[.ActionRef]]).
The generated workflow is `.github/workflows/observatory.yml`; it runs on pull
requests and manual dispatch. Install the selected tool and its dependencies in
that workflow when the standard Ubuntu runner does not already provide them.

Protocol: `[[.Protocol]]`. The reviewed `.observatory/config.json` scopes this
repository and workflow. Keep the same protocol, repository scope and optional
task aliases in the private collector's configuration. Public configuration
must contain no credentials, participant identities, activity or responses.

## Link a task

Create an issue with **Observatory study task**, then put `Closes #<number>` in
the implementation PR's description. One unambiguous closing issue produces a
stable task ID, `github-issue-<repository-id>-<issue-number>`. Missing API access,
missing links and multiple closing issues leave task identity unknown. Explicit
aliases can be registered in the config when the study needs another ID.
GitHub actor, triggering actor and event remain separate from declared
controller/session provenance. The generated workflow declares controller
unknown; it does not identify a human from a GitHub account.

## Observe the selected command

The generated workflow wraps only the command supplied during installation.
Other tools, jobs and workstation work need their own wrappers or observations.
Configuration and task-resolution files are designated hashed inputs. Each job
publishes its own immutable start/completion receipts. Publication after a
failed command is attempted, but runner loss can prevent delivery.

The collector must compare receipts with GitHub run, attempt and job metadata
and preserve failed, cancelled, skipped and incompletely observed executions.
Run discovery again before artifacts expire. The generated retention policy is
the action default; verify it against the study's durable collection schedule.

## Configure private effort collection

Follow the pinned [private runner guide](https://github.com/emmett08/observatory-instrumentation/blob/[[.ActionRef]]/docs/private-runner.md).
Use a private control repository and trusted runner. Keep raw activity, source
configuration, participant forms and responses in private storage. Public
repositories receive only deliberately published aggregate reports.

The optional effort-observation issue form records a declared summary. It is
separate from the hash-bound randomized review forms used by the estimator.
Human estimates remain unavailable until actual observations support them.
CI duration is tool runtime and is never converted into human labour.

## Updates

The action is pinned to `[[.ActionRef]]`; review a new full commit before changing
it. Rerunning installation is idempotent only when generated files are identical.
Existing customised files are never overwritten. Adapt the proposed workflow in
an ordinary reviewed PR when adding dependencies, matrices or more wrappers.
